-- ============================================================================
-- DC26 - Pore Pressure PROFESSIONAL (intermediate tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (porepressure, intermediate) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its
-- ACTIVE academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/porepressure/intermediate/manifest.json (emitted by a
-- generator, not hand-typed), and seeding the six module quiz banks plus the
-- final exam. Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons: from departure to pressure, the Eaton ratio, the
-- prognosis down the well, the trend lever, fracture pressure, and the
-- prognosis workflow.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the porepressure engines through
-- src/lib/porepressureTeaching.js (computeEatonExplorer and the untouched
-- computePrognosis capstone driver) and reproduces the live NG9 Professional
-- capstone answer key: onset 2520 m (tol 0, the 0.05 MPa rule on the 10 m
-- grid), NCT at TD 259.5530276341839 us/m, pore pressure 33.307730125 MPa at
-- 3000 m and 47.408579625 at TD, overpressure exactly 6 MPa, fracture
-- pressure 76.55157117548856 MPa at K = nu/(1-nu) = 2/3. eatonLab.test.js
-- pins the panel math to those same values.
--
-- Tier positioning: the Associate tier (DC11) owns the FRAME (hydrostatic
-- 41.408579625 MPa and overburden 91.12306695073282 at TD, Gardner, the NCT
-- and its exact fit 650.0000000000014 / 0.7000000000000015 per km) and
-- forward-quotes the 6 MPa TD overpressure and n = 3. Nothing here re-teaches
-- the frame or presents the forward quotes as discoveries. This tier owns the
-- INVERSION: the ratio (0.9580337483265022 at TD, cubed 0.8793108342707514),
-- the stress budget (49.714487325732826 MPa at TD), the detection rule (the
-- onset is 2520 not 2500, and moves with threshold AND exponent: 2540/2520/
-- 2510 across n 1..5), the closed loop (ramp recovered to 2.24e-8 Pa across
-- all 401 samples), the trend lever (the fitted trend doubles the TD
-- overpressure to 12.429177480013587 MPa and manufactures a spurious onset at
-- 120 m, worst ramp error 6.497 MPa at 3640 m), and the fracture ceiling
-- (mixture form: two thirds overburden plus one third pore pressure; one
-- third of any floor move passes to the ceiling). The n = 1.2 graded value
-- belongs to DC27 and is not keyed in this bank.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew, within-pool near-duplicates and
-- same-claim option pairs before seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct
-- option is longest in 15 pct and shortest in 12 pct.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on
-- re-seeds.
--
-- Ladder note: an INTERMEDIATE enrollment needs an unrevoked ASSOCIATE
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a porepressure
-- associate cert in-transaction, and a P3b check proves the porepressure
-- Associate tier is left undisturbed at 132 questions.
--
-- New pp-eaton-explorer panel. NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('porepressure', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-from-departure-to-pressure","title":"From Departure to Pressure","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-one-well-two-trends","l03-undercompaction-to-pressure","l04-the-prognosis-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-the-eaton-ratio","title":"The Eaton Ratio","lesson_keys":["l01-the-ratio","l02-the-stress-budget","l03-the-exponent","l04-worked-pp-at-3000","l05-what-the-method-cannot-see"]},{"key":"m03-the-prognosis-down-the-well","title":"The Prognosis Down the Well","lesson_keys":["l01-the-full-curve","l02-the-onset-and-the-detection-rule","l03-the-closed-loop","l04-the-td-numbers","l05-between-the-graded-depths"]},{"key":"m04-the-trend-lever","title":"The Trend Is the Lever","lesson_keys":["l01-two-trends-again","l02-the-fitted-trend-prognosis","l03-why-the-lever-is-so-long","l04-defending-a-trend"]},{"key":"m05-fracture-pressure","title":"Fracture Pressure","lesson_keys":["l01-why-fracture-pressure-now","l02-the-coefficient-form","l03-fp-down-the-well","l04-what-k-hides"]},{"key":"m06-the-prognosis-workflow","title":"The Prognosis Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-onward-to-expert"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
